## DATA PERSISTENCE & MIGRATION (CRITICAL — USER DATA PROTECTION)
- Use SwiftData as the primary persistence layer.
- **It is extremely important to migrate user data on every data model change.** Users must NEVER lose their data when updating to newer versions of the app.
- When modifying any @Model:
  - Always create a new schema version (e.g. Schema v2, v3, etc.).
  - Implement lightweight migration when possible.
  - For complex changes, define a custom MigrationPlan that explicitly maps old → new models, handles renames, default values, deletions, etc.
  - Update the ModelContainer configuration to include the migration plan.
  - Test the full migration path thoroughly before shipping.
- Never rely solely on implicit migration for production apps.
- Use @Model with proper relationships, unique constraints, and delete rules.
- All persistence operations must use async/await and be properly MainActor-isolated when updating UI.